/T (This course aims to equip students with the skills to conduct scientific research by introducing them to research methods and providing the basic skills needed to write academic research. Topics include defining the research problem and variables, identifying research significance and objectives, developing research models based on literature review, determining study population and sampling methods, data collection, hypothesis writing and testing, statistical analysis and interpretation, and writing conclusions and recommendations linked to the literature. The course also introduces students to various documentation and citation methods.)
/E (This course aims to equip students with the skills to conduct scientific research by introducing them to research methods and providing the basic skills needed to write academic research. Topics include defining the research problem and variables, identifying research significance and objectives, developing research models based on literature review, determining study population and sampling methods, data collection, hypothesis writing and testing, statistical analysis and interpretation, and writing conclusions and recommendations linked to the literature. The course also introduces students to various documentation and citation methods.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
